NAME

ulibGetSharedData - Returns a pointer to Xenolink's shared data segment


SYNOPSIS

struct SharedData *ulibGetSharedData()


DESCRIPTION

This function returns a pointer to Xenolink's shared data segment, or NULL
if the operation is unsuccessful or the Xenolink Manager is not running.

The shared data segment pointer was important under Z.3, but no longer
retains its importance under Z.4, since almost all system structures can
now be accessed via xenolink.library calls, rather than directly through
Xenolink's shared data segment.

However, ensuring that ulibGetSharedData() does not return NULL is a good
way to ensure that Xenolink is running.

If ulibGetSharedData() does return NULL, it means that the system
configuration has not been read into memory; all but the most trivial
xenolink.library functions will not work if this is the case.


NOTES

Xenolink no longer has a Shared->AmigaDOS2 flag (indicating AmigaDOS 2.0 or
later), since Xenolink, as of version Z.4, requires at least AmigaDOS 2.0 to
run.


RETURNS

NULL     - Xenolink Manager not running (configuration not read)
Non-zero - Xenolink fully operational
           (returns a pointer to a (struct SharedData), which is only useful
            under Xenolink Z.3 and earlier).
